<!DOCTYPE html>
<%# The hotel — not Hospello — is the brand throughout this namespace: body
    style carries the hotel's own colors as CSS custom properties
    (BrandingHelper#hotel_brand_style), and "Powered by Hospello" only
    appears where each view opts in via hotel.powered_by_visible.

    lang/dir follow I18n.locale, which every guest controller activates
    before rendering (see GuestLocalization) — so a guest who picked Arabic
    gets a genuinely right-to-left page, not just right-to-left text inside
    an left-to-right shell. Every layout rule below uses CSS *logical*
    properties (Tailwind's ps-/pe-/ms-/me-/text-start utilities, not
    pl-/pr-/ml-/mr-/text-left) so this one stylesheet serves both
    directions — "start"/"end" flip automatically with dir, "left"/"right"
    never would. %>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale %>" dir="<%= GuestLocaleHelper.rtl?(I18n.locale) ? "rtl" : "ltr" %>">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || Current.hotel&.name || "Hospello" %></title>
    <%# viewport-fit=cover lets the composer's safe-area padding reach the
        iPhone home indicator instead of stopping short of it.

        interactive-widget=resizes-content makes the on-screen keyboard shrink
        the viewport rather than float over the page. Without it the composer
        keeps its position in a viewport the keyboard is now covering, so the
        field the guest is typing into is behind the keyboard — the thing that
        makes a phone chat feel broken even when everything else is right. %>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover,interactive-widget=resizes-content">
    <%# Paints Safari's top bar and Chrome's address bar in the hotel's own
        colour. See BrandingHelper#hotel_theme_color for why this is as close
        to full screen as a QR-scanned page can get. %>
    <% if Current.hotel %>
      <meta name="theme-color" content="<%= hotel_theme_color(Current.hotel) %>">
    <% end %>
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%= yield :head %>

    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icon.png">

    <%# Includes all stylesheet files in app/assets/stylesheets %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>

  <%# hotel_brand_style already returns an html_safe "--brand-*:...;" string;
      falling back to "" (not omitting the attribute) when there is no
      resolved hotel yet (Guest::BaseController's re-entry page, hit before
      any tenant is known) keeps this one line instead of two branches. %>
  <%# body_class exists for one page: the chat pins the body so the document
      itself cannot scroll, because a fixed-height shell inside a growing body
      still leaves the whole page draggable — the composer stays put while
      everything behind it slides, which is worse than either. The landing
      page is a form and must keep scrolling normally, so this is opt-in
      rather than a change to the shared default. %>
  <%# The page's own height class REPLACES min-h-screen rather than joining it.
      Both would apply otherwise, and min-height:100vh beats height:100dvh on
      any phone whose toolbars retract — 100vh is the taller, retracted-chrome
      measurement — so the body ends up ~20px past the viewport and the whole
      page can be dragged behind a composer that is correctly pinned. Measured
      at exactly 20px, and it is the difference between a screen that feels
      solid and one that feels loose. %>
  <body class="<%= content_for(:body_class).presence || "min-h-screen" %> bg-gray-50 text-gray-900"
        style="<%= Current.hotel ? hotel_brand_style(Current.hotel) : "" %>">
    <% if notice = flash[:notice] %>
      <p class="mx-auto max-w-md px-4 pt-4 text-sm font-medium text-green-700" id="notice"><%= notice %></p>
    <% end %>
    <% if alert = flash[:alert] %>
      <p class="mx-auto max-w-md px-4 pt-4 text-sm font-medium text-red-600" id="alert"><%= alert %></p>
    <% end %>

    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
